{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T15:18:36.948Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"b2ed10cbfe9ede2fb711f0a0","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"ops-tdot"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Deep CI fails the release section gate when a release tag lands while a queued run holds an older main snapshot"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The deep tier's coverage run failed verify-release-changelog-sections on all four legs of run 45008656889: 'required release version 2026.11.22 has no usable changelog section'. The run was created at 09:40Z with main's snapshot from before the v2026.11.22 release, its jobs started on local runners only after the release had already pushed the tag, and the gate audited every tag in the fetched repository instead of only the tags reachable from the snapshot under audit. Root cause: the verifier's default inventory must scope release tags to those reachable from the checked-out HEAD; the pending package version already covers the pre-tagging release job. Fix scripts/verify-release-changelog-sections.ts and add a regression test that encodes the queued-snapshot race with a must-fail control."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-23T15:18:36.948Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T15:18:36.948Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex-agent"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":